window.CURRENT_TASK={"task_id": "L1-FUC-054-A1", "layer": "L1", "target_id": "FUC-054", "artifact_id": "FUC-054-A1", "title": "FUC-054 Publish Subsurface Surveillance and Acoustic Contact Reports / A1", "protocol_version": "L1_final_semantic_verified_candidate_v2", "artifact_sha256": "defde21e52517236c89fec1052b8a18c694e42840932eaa9af321364542ea538", "source_sha256": "40e0827f373b73731838c63950f540172969d6c83af6ebea4de3c9f3f5722e99", "reference_sha256": null, "reference_origin": null, "instructions": "<pre>只依据本断言允许且实际提供的引用证据的并集判断，不使用其他页面或常识补充。entailment=所有实质内容获支持；contradiction=直接矛盾；neutral=有实质内容无支持且不矛盾。槽位适配独立判断。无合法引用填写 NO_VALID_CITATION，不得猜测支持。保留审计候选断言原边界，不用最终槽位代替。</pre>", "material_html": "<h3>Publish Subsurface Surveillance and Acoustic Contact Reports</h3><p>给定参与者：C2 JU</p><p>按逐断言所列证据作答。最终槽位仅用于组织者计算 ESC；不替代审计候选。</p>", "groups": [{"key": "claims", "title": "逐断言评价", "fields": [{"key": "citation", "label": "引用状态", "type": "select", "required": true, "options": ["VALID", "NO_VALID_CITATION", "TECHNICAL_ISSUE"]}, {"key": "entailment", "label": "来源蕴含", "type": "select", "required": true, "options": ["entailment", "contradiction", "neutral", "NO_VALID_CITATION", "TECHNICAL_ISSUE"]}, {"key": "slot_fit", "label": "槽位适配", "type": "select", "required": true, "options": ["true", "false", "NOT_EVALUATED", "TECHNICAL_ISSUE"]}, {"key": "reason", "label": "证据判断理由", "type": "textarea", "required": true}, {"key": "slot_reason", "label": "槽位判断理由", "type": "textarea", "required": true}], "rows": [{"title": "goal:0", "html": "<pre>To report subsurface surveillance tracks and acoustic bearings/ranges derived from ASW sensors via J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track and J5.4 Acoustic Bearing/Range messages.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182, milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180, milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182, milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180, milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182</h4><pre>a. The information on the track is as complete, accurate, and timely as possible.\nb. The proper rules for reporting a track are followed.\n4.4.5.2 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) SURVEILLANCE REPORTING\nThe J3.0, J3.4, and J5.4 messages are used to exchange tactically significant information that has been derived from ASW sensors. Within the Subsurface surveillance function these messages are used to report bearings, ranges, and tracks.\n4.4.5.2.1 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) TRACK REPORTING\nThe rules for Subsurface surveillance track reporting are:\na. The source of track data shall be provided (Source TN).\nb. Established local tracks shall be reported with all known parameters at the next reporting opportunity.\nc. All data shall be time tagged.\n4.4.5.2.2 ACOUSTIC BEARING/RANGE REPORTING\nThe J5.</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180</h4><pre>System design should allow for longer wait times as well as an override in cases where operational necessity requires a shorter wait time or none at all.\n4.4.5 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) SURVEILLANCE\nThe rules and conventions applicable to reporting Subsurface (Maritime) surveillance information are based upon the requirements for exchanging these data between JUs but differ from those for Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) reporting due to the nature of the source of the information. The specific message used to report Subsurface surveillance tracks is the J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message. The relationship of acoustic and ASW point to Subsurface track reports is described in paragraphs 4.8.4 and 4.8.4.2.</pre><p>原始页位置：[54]</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</h4><pre>4 Acoustic Bearing/Range message shall be used to exchange information on bearings (ambiguous and resolved) and/or range derived from ASW sensors. The source frequency is not required to report acoustic information. Bearings shall be reported from the detecting sensor origin.\na. The J5.4E0 Latitude and Longitude fields shall be set to the position of the acoustic bearing origin.\nb. If the detecting sensor is integral to the reporting JU, the J5.4C2 Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the reporting JU. A towed array is considered integral to the ship. If the detecting sensor is integral to another unit, track, or point (e.g., non-IU, sonobuoy) being reported, the Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the detecting unit, track, or point.\nMIL-STD-6016B\n4-201</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p>"}, {"title": "preconditions:0", "html": "<pre>Tactically significant subsurface surveillance information derived from ASW sensors (bearings, ranges, or tracks) is available to be exchanged.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182</h4><pre>a. The information on the track is as complete, accurate, and timely as possible.\nb. The proper rules for reporting a track are followed.\n4.4.5.2 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) SURVEILLANCE REPORTING\nThe J3.0, J3.4, and J5.4 messages are used to exchange tactically significant information that has been derived from ASW sensors. Within the Subsurface surveillance function these messages are used to report bearings, ranges, and tracks.\n4.4.5.2.1 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) TRACK REPORTING\nThe rules for Subsurface surveillance track reporting are:\na. The source of track data shall be provided (Source TN).\nb. Established local tracks shall be reported with all known parameters at the next reporting opportunity.\nc. All data shall be time tagged.\n4.4.5.2.2 ACOUSTIC BEARING/RANGE REPORTING\nThe J5.</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p>"}, {"title": "preconditions:1", "html": "<pre>For subsurface track reporting, the source of track data is available for the Source TN and all data to be reported are time tagged.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182</h4><pre>a. The information on the track is as complete, accurate, and timely as possible.\nb. The proper rules for reporting a track are followed.\n4.4.5.2 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) SURVEILLANCE REPORTING\nThe J3.0, J3.4, and J5.4 messages are used to exchange tactically significant information that has been derived from ASW sensors. Within the Subsurface surveillance function these messages are used to report bearings, ranges, and tracks.\n4.4.5.2.1 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) TRACK REPORTING\nThe rules for Subsurface surveillance track reporting are:\na. The source of track data shall be provided (Source TN).\nb. Established local tracks shall be reported with all known parameters at the next reporting opportunity.\nc. All data shall be time tagged.\n4.4.5.2.2 ACOUSTIC BEARING/RANGE REPORTING\nThe J5.</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p>"}, {"title": "preconditions:2", "html": "<pre>For acoustic bearing/range reporting, bearing/range information derived from ASW sensors is available, and the position of the acoustic bearing origin and the applicable Origin TN for the detecting sensor are known.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</h4><pre>4 Acoustic Bearing/Range message shall be used to exchange information on bearings (ambiguous and resolved) and/or range derived from ASW sensors. The source frequency is not required to report acoustic information. Bearings shall be reported from the detecting sensor origin.\na. The J5.4E0 Latitude and Longitude fields shall be set to the position of the acoustic bearing origin.\nb. If the detecting sensor is integral to the reporting JU, the J5.4C2 Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the reporting JU. A towed array is considered integral to the ship. If the detecting sensor is integral to another unit, track, or point (e.g., non-IU, sonobuoy) being reported, the Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the detecting unit, track, or point.\nMIL-STD-6016B\n4-201</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p>"}, {"title": "preconditions:3", "html": "<pre>Where a subsurface track is reported under a Track Number, the C2 JU has assumed reporting responsibility for that Track Number because it was the first JU to report the contact, or one of the allowed exceptions applies (a J7.0 Drop Track message containing the TN has been received, or a J3.4 message containing the TN has not been received for two consecutive periodic updates).</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197, milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197, milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197</h4><pre>4.4.5.10 SUBSURFACE TRACK REPORTING RESPONSIBILITY\nSubsurface track reporting responsibility procedures are different from those for Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) tracks. It is often desirable that more than one JU report the same Subsurface contact using different TNs. This is to ensure continuity of reporting when contact is frequently lost/regained, and to allow comparison of different JUs&#x27; data to localize and identify contacts. The following are the $\\mathbb { R } ^ { 2 }$ rules for Subsurface tracks:\na. The first JU to report a contact assumes reporting responsibility for that Track Number. No other JU shall report the contact using that track number, unless one of the following occurs:\n(1) A J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message is received containing the TN.\n(2) A J3.</pre><p>原始页位置：[61]</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198</h4><pre>4 message containing the TN is not received for two consecutive periodic updates.\nb. Any other JU may report what it believes to be the same contact using a different TN. When this is done, only locally derived data shall be reported in the J3.4 message, i.e., the J3.4 messages shall not contain data derived only by the reception of remote data from other IU(s) reporting the same contact.\n4.4.5.11 REPORTING INACTIVE INTERFACE UNITS AS SUBSURFACE SURVEILLANCE TRACKS\nWhen a JU determines that a Subsurface IU is no longer active on the interface and the JU also holds local data on the IU, it shall assume $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ by reporting a J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message using the inactive IU address as the reference TN.</pre><p>原始页位置：[61]</p>"}, {"title": "trigger:0", "html": "<pre>Tactically significant subsurface surveillance information derived from ASW sensors—an established local track at the next reporting opportunity or acoustic bearing/range information—is to be exchanged.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182, milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182, milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182</h4><pre>a. The information on the track is as complete, accurate, and timely as possible.\nb. The proper rules for reporting a track are followed.\n4.4.5.2 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) SURVEILLANCE REPORTING\nThe J3.0, J3.4, and J5.4 messages are used to exchange tactically significant information that has been derived from ASW sensors. Within the Subsurface surveillance function these messages are used to report bearings, ranges, and tracks.\n4.4.5.2.1 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) TRACK REPORTING\nThe rules for Subsurface surveillance track reporting are:\na. The source of track data shall be provided (Source TN).\nb. Established local tracks shall be reported with all known parameters at the next reporting opportunity.\nc. All data shall be time tagged.\n4.4.5.2.2 ACOUSTIC BEARING/RANGE REPORTING\nThe J5.</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</h4><pre>4 Acoustic Bearing/Range message shall be used to exchange information on bearings (ambiguous and resolved) and/or range derived from ASW sensors. The source frequency is not required to report acoustic information. Bearings shall be reported from the detecting sensor origin.\na. The J5.4E0 Latitude and Longitude fields shall be set to the position of the acoustic bearing origin.\nb. If the detecting sensor is integral to the reporting JU, the J5.4C2 Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the reporting JU. A towed array is considered integral to the ship. If the detecting sensor is integral to another unit, track, or point (e.g., non-IU, sonobuoy) being reported, the Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the detecting unit, track, or point.\nMIL-STD-6016B\n4-201</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:0", "html": "<pre>C² JU provides the source of track data as the Source TN.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182</h4><pre>a. The information on the track is as complete, accurate, and timely as possible.\nb. The proper rules for reporting a track are followed.\n4.4.5.2 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) SURVEILLANCE REPORTING\nThe J3.0, J3.4, and J5.4 messages are used to exchange tactically significant information that has been derived from ASW sensors. Within the Subsurface surveillance function these messages are used to report bearings, ranges, and tracks.\n4.4.5.2.1 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) TRACK REPORTING\nThe rules for Subsurface surveillance track reporting are:\na. The source of track data shall be provided (Source TN).\nb. Established local tracks shall be reported with all known parameters at the next reporting opportunity.\nc. All data shall be time tagged.\n4.4.5.2.2 ACOUSTIC BEARING/RANGE REPORTING\nThe J5.</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:1", "html": "<pre>C² JU time tags all Subsurface surveillance track data.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182</h4><pre>a. The information on the track is as complete, accurate, and timely as possible.\nb. The proper rules for reporting a track are followed.\n4.4.5.2 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) SURVEILLANCE REPORTING\nThe J3.0, J3.4, and J5.4 messages are used to exchange tactically significant information that has been derived from ASW sensors. Within the Subsurface surveillance function these messages are used to report bearings, ranges, and tracks.\n4.4.5.2.1 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) TRACK REPORTING\nThe rules for Subsurface surveillance track reporting are:\na. The source of track data shall be provided (Source TN).\nb. Established local tracks shall be reported with all known parameters at the next reporting opportunity.\nc. All data shall be time tagged.\n4.4.5.2.2 ACOUSTIC BEARING/RANGE REPORTING\nThe J5.</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:2", "html": "<pre>C² JU reports established local tracks with all known parameters at the next reporting opportunity using the J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182, milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182, milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182</h4><pre>a. The information on the track is as complete, accurate, and timely as possible.\nb. The proper rules for reporting a track are followed.\n4.4.5.2 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) SURVEILLANCE REPORTING\nThe J3.0, J3.4, and J5.4 messages are used to exchange tactically significant information that has been derived from ASW sensors. Within the Subsurface surveillance function these messages are used to report bearings, ranges, and tracks.\n4.4.5.2.1 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) TRACK REPORTING\nThe rules for Subsurface surveillance track reporting are:\na. The source of track data shall be provided (Source TN).\nb. Established local tracks shall be reported with all known parameters at the next reporting opportunity.\nc. All data shall be time tagged.\n4.4.5.2.2 ACOUSTIC BEARING/RANGE REPORTING\nThe J5.</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180</h4><pre>System design should allow for longer wait times as well as an override in cases where operational necessity requires a shorter wait time or none at all.\n4.4.5 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) SURVEILLANCE\nThe rules and conventions applicable to reporting Subsurface (Maritime) surveillance information are based upon the requirements for exchanging these data between JUs but differ from those for Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) reporting due to the nature of the source of the information. The specific message used to report Subsurface surveillance tracks is the J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message. The relationship of acoustic and ASW point to Subsurface track reports is described in paragraphs 4.8.4 and 4.8.4.2.</pre><p>原始页位置：[54]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:3", "html": "<pre>C² JU reports the geodetic latitude and longitude for each Subsurface surveillance track in the J3.4 message and specifies depth when available.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195</h4><pre>4.4.5.4 POSITIONAL DATA\nThe geodetic latitude and longitude for each Subsurface surveillance track shall be reported in the J3.4 message. In addition, Subsurface surveillance reporting shall include the capability for specifying depth when available.\n4.4.5.5 VELOCITY\nThe velocity of Subsurface surveillance tracks shall be reported as course and speed. The speed shall be reported in data miles per hour of ground speed. The course shall be reported in degrees with respect to true north.\n4.4.5.6 IDENTITY DATA\nTrack identity, as defined in paragraph 4.4.2.1, is exchanged using the Identity field. Platform and Platform Activity may also be reported in the J3.4I message to further amplify the identity of the reported track in accordance with paragraph 4.4.2.1.3.\n4.4.5.</pre><p>原始页位置：[60]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:4", "html": "<pre>C² JU reports the velocity of Subsurface surveillance tracks as course and speed, with speed in data miles per hour of ground speed and course in degrees with respect to true north.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195</h4><pre>4.4.5.4 POSITIONAL DATA\nThe geodetic latitude and longitude for each Subsurface surveillance track shall be reported in the J3.4 message. In addition, Subsurface surveillance reporting shall include the capability for specifying depth when available.\n4.4.5.5 VELOCITY\nThe velocity of Subsurface surveillance tracks shall be reported as course and speed. The speed shall be reported in data miles per hour of ground speed. The course shall be reported in degrees with respect to true north.\n4.4.5.6 IDENTITY DATA\nTrack identity, as defined in paragraph 4.4.2.1, is exchanged using the Identity field. Platform and Platform Activity may also be reported in the J3.4I message to further amplify the identity of the reported track in accordance with paragraph 4.4.2.1.3.\n4.4.5.</pre><p>原始页位置：[60]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:5", "html": "<pre>C² JU exchanges track identity using the Identity field and may report Platform and Platform Activity in the J3.4I message.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195</h4><pre>4.4.5.4 POSITIONAL DATA\nThe geodetic latitude and longitude for each Subsurface surveillance track shall be reported in the J3.4 message. In addition, Subsurface surveillance reporting shall include the capability for specifying depth when available.\n4.4.5.5 VELOCITY\nThe velocity of Subsurface surveillance tracks shall be reported as course and speed. The speed shall be reported in data miles per hour of ground speed. The course shall be reported in degrees with respect to true north.\n4.4.5.6 IDENTITY DATA\nTrack identity, as defined in paragraph 4.4.2.1, is exchanged using the Identity field. Platform and Platform Activity may also be reported in the J3.4I message to further amplify the identity of the reported track in accordance with paragraph 4.4.2.1.3.\n4.4.5.</pre><p>原始页位置：[60]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:6", "html": "<pre>C² JU uses the J5.4 Acoustic Bearing/Range message to exchange information on bearings (ambiguous and resolved) and/or range derived from ASW sensors.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</h4><pre>4 Acoustic Bearing/Range message shall be used to exchange information on bearings (ambiguous and resolved) and/or range derived from ASW sensors. The source frequency is not required to report acoustic information. Bearings shall be reported from the detecting sensor origin.\na. The J5.4E0 Latitude and Longitude fields shall be set to the position of the acoustic bearing origin.\nb. If the detecting sensor is integral to the reporting JU, the J5.4C2 Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the reporting JU. A towed array is considered integral to the ship. If the detecting sensor is integral to another unit, track, or point (e.g., non-IU, sonobuoy) being reported, the Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the detecting unit, track, or point.\nMIL-STD-6016B\n4-201</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:7", "html": "<pre>C² JU sets the J5.4E0 Latitude and Longitude fields to the position of the acoustic bearing origin and reports bearings from the detecting sensor origin.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</h4><pre>4 Acoustic Bearing/Range message shall be used to exchange information on bearings (ambiguous and resolved) and/or range derived from ASW sensors. The source frequency is not required to report acoustic information. Bearings shall be reported from the detecting sensor origin.\na. The J5.4E0 Latitude and Longitude fields shall be set to the position of the acoustic bearing origin.\nb. If the detecting sensor is integral to the reporting JU, the J5.4C2 Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the reporting JU. A towed array is considered integral to the ship. If the detecting sensor is integral to another unit, track, or point (e.g., non-IU, sonobuoy) being reported, the Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the detecting unit, track, or point.\nMIL-STD-6016B\n4-201</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:8", "html": "<pre>If the detecting sensor is integral to the reporting JU, C² JU sets the J5.4C2 Origin TN field to the TN of the reporting JU (a towed array is considered integral to the ship); if the detecting sensor is integral to another unit, track, or point being reported, C² JU sets the Origin TN field to the TN of the detecting unit, track, or point.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</h4><pre>4 Acoustic Bearing/Range message shall be used to exchange information on bearings (ambiguous and resolved) and/or range derived from ASW sensors. The source frequency is not required to report acoustic information. Bearings shall be reported from the detecting sensor origin.\na. The J5.4E0 Latitude and Longitude fields shall be set to the position of the acoustic bearing origin.\nb. If the detecting sensor is integral to the reporting JU, the J5.4C2 Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the reporting JU. A towed array is considered integral to the ship. If the detecting sensor is integral to another unit, track, or point (e.g., non-IU, sonobuoy) being reported, the Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the detecting unit, track, or point.\nMIL-STD-6016B\n4-201</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:0", "html": "<pre>2a. If contact is lost and the operator decides to report the track as a DATUM, C² JU reports a J3.4 message with the same Reference TN as the track for which contact has been lost, sets Data Report Type (DRT) = 4 (DATUM), sets ASW Time Function = 3 (Time Contact Lost) or 1 (Time Datum Established), sets Hour and Minute to the truncated time contact was lost or DATUM established, and includes Latitude, Longitude, and 15 Meters Depth; the decision to report a DATUM is an operator function.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190</h4><pre>or the reported Subsurface surveillance fix or other ASW point may be associated with an existing track.\n4.4.5.2.5 REPORTING SUBSURFACE SURVEILLANCE TRACK DATUM\nC² JUs that report subsurface tracks shall have the capability to report a track as a DATUM when contact is lost. The following protocols apply:\na. The decision to report a DATUM shall be an operator function.\nb. The DATUM shall be reported in a J3.4 message with the same Reference TN as the track for which contact has been lost, and the other J3.4 fields set as follows:\n(1) Data Report Type (DRT) = 4 (DATUM).\n(2) ASW Time Function = 3 (Time Contact Lost) or 1 (Time Datum Established).\n(3) Hour and Minute: Time (truncated) that contact was lost or DATUM established.\n(4) Latitude, Longitude, 15 Meters Depth,</pre><p>原始页位置：[58]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:1", "html": "<pre>2b. If contact is regained after a DATUM, C² JU reports a J3.4 with DRT set to value 0, 1, or 2 using the same TN as the DATUM, or a new TN depending on operator action.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193</h4><pre>If contact is regained, a J3.4 with DRT set to value 0, 1 or 2 shall be reported with the same TN as the DATUM, or a new TN depending on operator action.\n4.4.5.3 TRACK ASSOCIATION\nBecause Subsurface (Maritime) surveillance is performed using different information sources than those used for Air, Surface (Maritime), or Land (Ground) surveillance (e.g., Radar or IFF/SIF transponder), the correlation procedures which are specified for Air, Surface (Maritime), or Land (Ground) tracks are not applied to Subsurface tracks. Instead, it is the function of the operator to perform manual correlation of Subsurface surveillance data. In order to provide for a complete compilation of the subsurface situation, the J7.</pre><p>原始页位置：[59]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:2", "html": "<pre>2c. If another JU has already reported the contact under a Track Number and either a J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message containing the TN is received or a J3.4 message containing the TN has not been received for two consecutive periodic updates, C² JU may report the contact using that track number.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197, milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197, milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197</h4><pre>4.4.5.10 SUBSURFACE TRACK REPORTING RESPONSIBILITY\nSubsurface track reporting responsibility procedures are different from those for Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) tracks. It is often desirable that more than one JU report the same Subsurface contact using different TNs. This is to ensure continuity of reporting when contact is frequently lost/regained, and to allow comparison of different JUs&#x27; data to localize and identify contacts. The following are the $\\mathbb { R } ^ { 2 }$ rules for Subsurface tracks:\na. The first JU to report a contact assumes reporting responsibility for that Track Number. No other JU shall report the contact using that track number, unless one of the following occurs:\n(1) A J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message is received containing the TN.\n(2) A J3.</pre><p>原始页位置：[61]</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198</h4><pre>4 message containing the TN is not received for two consecutive periodic updates.\nb. Any other JU may report what it believes to be the same contact using a different TN. When this is done, only locally derived data shall be reported in the J3.4 message, i.e., the J3.4 messages shall not contain data derived only by the reception of remote data from other IU(s) reporting the same contact.\n4.4.5.11 REPORTING INACTIVE INTERFACE UNITS AS SUBSURFACE SURVEILLANCE TRACKS\nWhen a JU determines that a Subsurface IU is no longer active on the interface and the JU also holds local data on the IU, it shall assume $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ by reporting a J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message using the inactive IU address as the reference TN.</pre><p>原始页位置：[61]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:3", "html": "<pre>2d. If C² JU believes a contact is the same contact reported by another JU using a different TN, C² JU may report it using a different TN; when this is done, only locally derived data shall be reported in the J3.4 message, and the J3.4 messages shall not contain data derived only by the reception of remote data from other IU(s) reporting the same contact.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198</h4><pre>4 message containing the TN is not received for two consecutive periodic updates.\nb. Any other JU may report what it believes to be the same contact using a different TN. When this is done, only locally derived data shall be reported in the J3.4 message, i.e., the J3.4 messages shall not contain data derived only by the reception of remote data from other IU(s) reporting the same contact.\n4.4.5.11 REPORTING INACTIVE INTERFACE UNITS AS SUBSURFACE SURVEILLANCE TRACKS\nWhen a JU determines that a Subsurface IU is no longer active on the interface and the JU also holds local data on the IU, it shall assume $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ by reporting a J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message using the inactive IU address as the reference TN.</pre><p>原始页位置：[61]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:4", "html": "<pre>2e. If C² JU determines that a Subsurface IU is no longer active on the interface and C² JU also holds local data on the IU, C² JU assumes R² by reporting a J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message using the inactive IU address as the reference TN.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198</h4><pre>4 message containing the TN is not received for two consecutive periodic updates.\nb. Any other JU may report what it believes to be the same contact using a different TN. When this is done, only locally derived data shall be reported in the J3.4 message, i.e., the J3.4 messages shall not contain data derived only by the reception of remote data from other IU(s) reporting the same contact.\n4.4.5.11 REPORTING INACTIVE INTERFACE UNITS AS SUBSURFACE SURVEILLANCE TRACKS\nWhen a JU determines that a Subsurface IU is no longer active on the interface and the JU also holds local data on the IU, it shall assume $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ by reporting a J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message using the inactive IU address as the reference TN.</pre><p>原始页位置：[61]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:5", "html": "<pre>2f. If further refined information concerning a subsurface fix or one of the other ASW points may result in a Subsurface surveillance track, C² JU reports the track with a new TN.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189</h4><pre>row spacing, pattern radius, and/or bearing may be reported as necessary. For Limiting Line of Approach the bearing and time of activation will be reported. For ASW Station, the time of activation will be reported.\nMinimum implementation requirements for each ASW point amplification value is specified in Appendix A. Word sequence requirements are specified in T/R rules and message maps.\n4.4.5.2.4 ESTABLISHMENT OF SUBSURFACE SURVEILLANCE TRACKS AND POINTS AND FIXES\nFurther refined information concerning a subsurface fix or one of the other ASW points reported as specified in paragraph 4.4.5.2.3 above may result in a Subsurface surveillance track which would then be reported with a new TN,</pre><p>原始页位置：[58]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:6", "html": "<pre>2g. When associating Subsurface surveillance data, C² JU performs manual correlation of Subsurface surveillance data; the correlation procedures specified for Air, Surface (Maritime), or Land (Ground) tracks are not applied to Subsurface tracks.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193</h4><pre>If contact is regained, a J3.4 with DRT set to value 0, 1 or 2 shall be reported with the same TN as the DATUM, or a new TN depending on operator action.\n4.4.5.3 TRACK ASSOCIATION\nBecause Subsurface (Maritime) surveillance is performed using different information sources than those used for Air, Surface (Maritime), or Land (Ground) surveillance (e.g., Radar or IFF/SIF transponder), the correlation procedures which are specified for Air, Surface (Maritime), or Land (Ground) tracks are not applied to Subsurface tracks. Instead, it is the function of the operator to perform manual correlation of Subsurface surveillance data. In order to provide for a complete compilation of the subsurface situation, the J7.</pre><p>原始页位置：[59]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:7", "html": "<pre>2h. If operational necessity requires a shorter wait time or none at all, an override is allowed; system design should also allow for longer wait times.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180</h4><pre>System design should allow for longer wait times as well as an override in cases where operational necessity requires a shorter wait time or none at all.\n4.4.5 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) SURVEILLANCE\nThe rules and conventions applicable to reporting Subsurface (Maritime) surveillance information are based upon the requirements for exchanging these data between JUs but differ from those for Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) reporting due to the nature of the source of the information. The specific message used to report Subsurface surveillance tracks is the J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message. The relationship of acoustic and ASW point to Subsurface track reports is described in paragraphs 4.8.4 and 4.8.4.2.</pre><p>原始页位置：[54]</p>"}, {"title": "exception_flow:0", "html": "<pre>1. If contact is lost while reporting a Subsurface surveillance track and the operator decides to report the track as a DATUM, C² JU reports a J3.4 message with the same Reference TN as the track for which contact has been lost, sets Data Report Type (DRT) = 4 (DATUM), sets ASW Time Function = 3 (Time Contact Lost) or 1 (Time Datum Established), sets Hour and Minute to the truncated time contact was lost or DATUM established, and includes Latitude, Longitude, and 15 Meters Depth; the decision to report a DATUM is an operator function. Exit: the DATUM report is sent as a J3.4 message.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190</h4><pre>or the reported Subsurface surveillance fix or other ASW point may be associated with an existing track.\n4.4.5.2.5 REPORTING SUBSURFACE SURVEILLANCE TRACK DATUM\nC² JUs that report subsurface tracks shall have the capability to report a track as a DATUM when contact is lost. The following protocols apply:\na. The decision to report a DATUM shall be an operator function.\nb. The DATUM shall be reported in a J3.4 message with the same Reference TN as the track for which contact has been lost, and the other J3.4 fields set as follows:\n(1) Data Report Type (DRT) = 4 (DATUM).\n(2) ASW Time Function = 3 (Time Contact Lost) or 1 (Time Datum Established).\n(3) Hour and Minute: Time (truncated) that contact was lost or DATUM established.\n(4) Latitude, Longitude, 15 Meters Depth,</pre><p>原始页位置：[58]</p>"}, {"title": "exception_flow:1", "html": "<pre>2. If contact is regained after a DATUM, C² JU reports a J3.4 with DRT set to value 0, 1, or 2 using the same TN as the DATUM, or a new TN depending on operator action. Exit: contact reporting resumes with the selected DRT and TN.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193</h4><pre>If contact is regained, a J3.4 with DRT set to value 0, 1 or 2 shall be reported with the same TN as the DATUM, or a new TN depending on operator action.\n4.4.5.3 TRACK ASSOCIATION\nBecause Subsurface (Maritime) surveillance is performed using different information sources than those used for Air, Surface (Maritime), or Land (Ground) surveillance (e.g., Radar or IFF/SIF transponder), the correlation procedures which are specified for Air, Surface (Maritime), or Land (Ground) tracks are not applied to Subsurface tracks. Instead, it is the function of the operator to perform manual correlation of Subsurface surveillance data. In order to provide for a complete compilation of the subsurface situation, the J7.</pre><p>原始页位置：[59]</p>"}, {"title": "exception_flow:2", "html": "<pre>3. If C² JU is not the first JU to report a contact and neither allowed exception occurs (a J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message containing the TN is received, or a J3.4 message containing the TN is not received for two consecutive periodic updates), C² JU shall not report the contact using that track number. Exit: C² JU may report what it believes to be the same contact using a different TN, and when this is done only locally derived data shall be reported in the J3.4 message.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197, milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197, milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197</h4><pre>4.4.5.10 SUBSURFACE TRACK REPORTING RESPONSIBILITY\nSubsurface track reporting responsibility procedures are different from those for Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) tracks. It is often desirable that more than one JU report the same Subsurface contact using different TNs. This is to ensure continuity of reporting when contact is frequently lost/regained, and to allow comparison of different JUs&#x27; data to localize and identify contacts. The following are the $\\mathbb { R } ^ { 2 }$ rules for Subsurface tracks:\na. The first JU to report a contact assumes reporting responsibility for that Track Number. No other JU shall report the contact using that track number, unless one of the following occurs:\n(1) A J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message is received containing the TN.\n(2) A J3.</pre><p>原始页位置：[61]</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198</h4><pre>4 message containing the TN is not received for two consecutive periodic updates.\nb. Any other JU may report what it believes to be the same contact using a different TN. When this is done, only locally derived data shall be reported in the J3.4 message, i.e., the J3.4 messages shall not contain data derived only by the reception of remote data from other IU(s) reporting the same contact.\n4.4.5.11 REPORTING INACTIVE INTERFACE UNITS AS SUBSURFACE SURVEILLANCE TRACKS\nWhen a JU determines that a Subsurface IU is no longer active on the interface and the JU also holds local data on the IU, it shall assume $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ by reporting a J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message using the inactive IU address as the reference TN.</pre><p>原始页位置：[61]</p>"}, {"title": "exception_flow:3", "html": "<pre>4. If C² JU determines that a Subsurface IU is no longer active on the interface and C² JU also holds local data on the IU, C² JU assumes R² by reporting a J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message using the inactive IU address as the reference TN. Exit: the J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message using the inactive IU address as the reference TN is sent.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198</h4><pre>4 message containing the TN is not received for two consecutive periodic updates.\nb. Any other JU may report what it believes to be the same contact using a different TN. When this is done, only locally derived data shall be reported in the J3.4 message, i.e., the J3.4 messages shall not contain data derived only by the reception of remote data from other IU(s) reporting the same contact.\n4.4.5.11 REPORTING INACTIVE INTERFACE UNITS AS SUBSURFACE SURVEILLANCE TRACKS\nWhen a JU determines that a Subsurface IU is no longer active on the interface and the JU also holds local data on the IU, it shall assume $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ by reporting a J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message using the inactive IU address as the reference TN.</pre><p>原始页位置：[61]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:0", "html": "<pre>Subsurface surveillance track information has been reported using the J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180</h4><pre>System design should allow for longer wait times as well as an override in cases where operational necessity requires a shorter wait time or none at all.\n4.4.5 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) SURVEILLANCE\nThe rules and conventions applicable to reporting Subsurface (Maritime) surveillance information are based upon the requirements for exchanging these data between JUs but differ from those for Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) reporting due to the nature of the source of the information. The specific message used to report Subsurface surveillance tracks is the J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message. The relationship of acoustic and ASW point to Subsurface track reports is described in paragraphs 4.8.4 and 4.8.4.2.</pre><p>原始页位置：[54]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:1", "html": "<pre>Acoustic bearing/range information derived from ASW sensors has been exchanged using the Acoustic Bearing/Range message.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</h4><pre>4 Acoustic Bearing/Range message shall be used to exchange information on bearings (ambiguous and resolved) and/or range derived from ASW sensors. The source frequency is not required to report acoustic information. Bearings shall be reported from the detecting sensor origin.\na. The J5.4E0 Latitude and Longitude fields shall be set to the position of the acoustic bearing origin.\nb. If the detecting sensor is integral to the reporting JU, the J5.4C2 Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the reporting JU. A towed array is considered integral to the ship. If the detecting sensor is integral to another unit, track, or point (e.g., non-IU, sonobuoy) being reported, the Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the detecting unit, track, or point.\nMIL-STD-6016B\n4-201</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:2", "html": "<pre>For reported Subsurface surveillance tracks, the source of track data has been provided as the Source TN; established local tracks have been reported with all known parameters at the next reporting opportunity; and all data have been time tagged.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182</h4><pre>a. The information on the track is as complete, accurate, and timely as possible.\nb. The proper rules for reporting a track are followed.\n4.4.5.2 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) SURVEILLANCE REPORTING\nThe J3.0, J3.4, and J5.4 messages are used to exchange tactically significant information that has been derived from ASW sensors. Within the Subsurface surveillance function these messages are used to report bearings, ranges, and tracks.\n4.4.5.2.1 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) TRACK REPORTING\nThe rules for Subsurface surveillance track reporting are:\na. The source of track data shall be provided (Source TN).\nb. Established local tracks shall be reported with all known parameters at the next reporting opportunity.\nc. All data shall be time tagged.\n4.4.5.2.2 ACOUSTIC BEARING/RANGE REPORTING\nThe J5.</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:3", "html": "<pre>The information on the track is as complete, accurate, and timely as possible, and the proper rules for reporting a track have been followed.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182</h4><pre>a. The information on the track is as complete, accurate, and timely as possible.\nb. The proper rules for reporting a track are followed.\n4.4.5.2 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) SURVEILLANCE REPORTING\nThe J3.0, J3.4, and J5.4 messages are used to exchange tactically significant information that has been derived from ASW sensors. Within the Subsurface surveillance function these messages are used to report bearings, ranges, and tracks.\n4.4.5.2.1 SUBSURFACE (MARITIME) TRACK REPORTING\nThe rules for Subsurface surveillance track reporting are:\na. The source of track data shall be provided (Source TN).\nb. Established local tracks shall be reported with all known parameters at the next reporting opportunity.\nc. All data shall be time tagged.\n4.4.5.2.2 ACOUSTIC BEARING/RANGE REPORTING\nThe J5.</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:4", "html": "<pre>For the Acoustic Bearing/Range report, the J5.4E0 Latitude and Longitude fields have been set to the position of the acoustic bearing origin, and bearings have been reported from the detecting sensor origin.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</h4><pre>4 Acoustic Bearing/Range message shall be used to exchange information on bearings (ambiguous and resolved) and/or range derived from ASW sensors. The source frequency is not required to report acoustic information. Bearings shall be reported from the detecting sensor origin.\na. The J5.4E0 Latitude and Longitude fields shall be set to the position of the acoustic bearing origin.\nb. If the detecting sensor is integral to the reporting JU, the J5.4C2 Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the reporting JU. A towed array is considered integral to the ship. If the detecting sensor is integral to another unit, track, or point (e.g., non-IU, sonobuoy) being reported, the Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the detecting unit, track, or point.\nMIL-STD-6016B\n4-201</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:5", "html": "<pre>For the Acoustic Bearing/Range report, if the detecting sensor is integral to the reporting JU, the J5.4C2 Origin TN field contains the TN of the reporting JU (a towed array is considered integral to the ship); if the detecting sensor is integral to another unit, track, or point being reported, the Origin TN field contains the TN of the detecting unit, track, or point.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183</h4><pre>4 Acoustic Bearing/Range message shall be used to exchange information on bearings (ambiguous and resolved) and/or range derived from ASW sensors. The source frequency is not required to report acoustic information. Bearings shall be reported from the detecting sensor origin.\na. The J5.4E0 Latitude and Longitude fields shall be set to the position of the acoustic bearing origin.\nb. If the detecting sensor is integral to the reporting JU, the J5.4C2 Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the reporting JU. A towed array is considered integral to the ship. If the detecting sensor is integral to another unit, track, or point (e.g., non-IU, sonobuoy) being reported, the Origin TN field shall contain the TN of the detecting unit, track, or point.\nMIL-STD-6016B\n4-201</pre><p>原始页位置：[55]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:6", "html": "<pre>If contact was lost and the operator decided to report the track as a DATUM, a J3.4 message has been reported with the same Reference TN as the track for which contact has been lost, DRT = 4 (DATUM), ASW Time Function = 3 (Time Contact Lost) or 1 (Time Datum Established), Hour and Minute set to the truncated time contact was lost or DATUM established, and Latitude, Longitude, and 15 Meters Depth included.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190</h4><pre>or the reported Subsurface surveillance fix or other ASW point may be associated with an existing track.\n4.4.5.2.5 REPORTING SUBSURFACE SURVEILLANCE TRACK DATUM\nC² JUs that report subsurface tracks shall have the capability to report a track as a DATUM when contact is lost. The following protocols apply:\na. The decision to report a DATUM shall be an operator function.\nb. The DATUM shall be reported in a J3.4 message with the same Reference TN as the track for which contact has been lost, and the other J3.4 fields set as follows:\n(1) Data Report Type (DRT) = 4 (DATUM).\n(2) ASW Time Function = 3 (Time Contact Lost) or 1 (Time Datum Established).\n(3) Hour and Minute: Time (truncated) that contact was lost or DATUM established.\n(4) Latitude, Longitude, 15 Meters Depth,</pre><p>原始页位置：[58]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:7", "html": "<pre>If contact was regained after a DATUM, a J3.4 message has been reported with DRT set to value 0, 1, or 2 using the same TN as the DATUM, or a new TN depending on operator action.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193</h4><pre>If contact is regained, a J3.4 with DRT set to value 0, 1 or 2 shall be reported with the same TN as the DATUM, or a new TN depending on operator action.\n4.4.5.3 TRACK ASSOCIATION\nBecause Subsurface (Maritime) surveillance is performed using different information sources than those used for Air, Surface (Maritime), or Land (Ground) surveillance (e.g., Radar or IFF/SIF transponder), the correlation procedures which are specified for Air, Surface (Maritime), or Land (Ground) tracks are not applied to Subsurface tracks. Instead, it is the function of the operator to perform manual correlation of Subsurface surveillance data. In order to provide for a complete compilation of the subsurface situation, the J7.</pre><p>原始页位置：[59]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:8", "html": "<pre>If C² JU determined that a Subsurface IU is no longer active on the interface and C² JU also holds local data on the IU, C² JU has assumed R² by reporting a J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message using the inactive IU address as the reference TN.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198</h4><pre>4 message containing the TN is not received for two consecutive periodic updates.\nb. Any other JU may report what it believes to be the same contact using a different TN. When this is done, only locally derived data shall be reported in the J3.4 message, i.e., the J3.4 messages shall not contain data derived only by the reception of remote data from other IU(s) reporting the same contact.\n4.4.5.11 REPORTING INACTIVE INTERFACE UNITS AS SUBSURFACE SURVEILLANCE TRACKS\nWhen a JU determines that a Subsurface IU is no longer active on the interface and the JU also holds local data on the IU, it shall assume $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ by reporting a J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message using the inactive IU address as the reference TN.</pre><p>原始页位置：[61]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:9", "html": "<pre>When C² JU reported what it believes to be the same contact using a different TN, only locally derived data have been reported in the J3.4 message, and the J3.4 messages do not contain data derived only by the reception of remote data from other IU(s) reporting the same contact.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198</h4><pre>4 message containing the TN is not received for two consecutive periodic updates.\nb. Any other JU may report what it believes to be the same contact using a different TN. When this is done, only locally derived data shall be reported in the J3.4 message, i.e., the J3.4 messages shall not contain data derived only by the reception of remote data from other IU(s) reporting the same contact.\n4.4.5.11 REPORTING INACTIVE INTERFACE UNITS AS SUBSURFACE SURVEILLANCE TRACKS\nWhen a JU determines that a Subsurface IU is no longer active on the interface and the JU also holds local data on the IU, it shall assume $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ by reporting a J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message using the inactive IU address as the reference TN.</pre><p>原始页位置：[61]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:10", "html": "<pre>If C² JU was the first JU to report a contact, C² JU has assumed reporting responsibility for that Track Number.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197</h4><pre>4.4.5.10 SUBSURFACE TRACK REPORTING RESPONSIBILITY\nSubsurface track reporting responsibility procedures are different from those for Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) tracks. It is often desirable that more than one JU report the same Subsurface contact using different TNs. This is to ensure continuity of reporting when contact is frequently lost/regained, and to allow comparison of different JUs&#x27; data to localize and identify contacts. The following are the $\\mathbb { R } ^ { 2 }$ rules for Subsurface tracks:\na. The first JU to report a contact assumes reporting responsibility for that Track Number. No other JU shall report the contact using that track number, unless one of the following occurs:\n(1) A J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message is received containing the TN.\n(2) A J3.</pre><p>原始页位置：[61]</p>"}], "repeat": false, "min_rows": 0}], "blockers": [], "claim_meta": [{"slot": "goal", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "To report subsurface surveillance tracks and acoustic bearings/ranges derived from ASW sensors via J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track and J5.4 Acoustic Bearing/Range messages.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "preconditions", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "Tactically significant subsurface surveillance information derived from ASW sensors (bearings, ranges, or tracks) is available to be exchanged.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C181", "milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "preconditions", "audit_ordinal": 1, "content": "For subsurface track reporting, the source of track data is available for the Source TN and all data to be reported are time tagged.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C181", "milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "preconditions", "audit_ordinal": 2, "content": "For acoustic bearing/range reporting, bearing/range information derived from ASW sensors is available, and the position of the acoustic bearing origin and the applicable Origin TN for the detecting sensor are known.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C181", "milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "preconditions", "audit_ordinal": 3, "content": "Where a subsurface track is reported under a Track Number, the C2 JU has assumed reporting responsibility for that Track Number because it was the first JU to report the contact, or one of the allowed exceptions applies (a J7.0 Drop Track message containing the TN has been received, or a J3.4 message containing the TN has not been received for two consecutive periodic updates).", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C181", "milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "trigger", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "Tactically significant subsurface surveillance information derived from ASW sensors—an established local track at the next reporting opportunity or acoustic bearing/range information—is to be exchanged.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C148", "milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C19", "milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "C² JU provides the source of track data as the Source TN.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 1, "content": "C² JU time tags all Subsurface surveillance track data.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 2, "content": "C² JU reports established local tracks with all known parameters at the next reporting opportunity using the J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 3, "content": "C² JU reports the geodetic latitude and longitude for each Subsurface surveillance track in the J3.4 message and specifies depth when available.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 4, "content": "C² JU reports the velocity of Subsurface surveillance tracks as course and speed, with speed in data miles per hour of ground speed and course in degrees with respect to true north.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 5, "content": "C² JU exchanges track identity using the Identity field and may report Platform and Platform Activity in the J3.4I message.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 6, "content": "C² JU uses the J5.4 Acoustic Bearing/Range message to exchange information on bearings (ambiguous and resolved) and/or range derived from ASW sensors.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 7, "content": "C² JU sets the J5.4E0 Latitude and Longitude fields to the position of the acoustic bearing origin and reports bearings from the detecting sensor origin.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 8, "content": "If the detecting sensor is integral to the reporting JU, C² JU sets the J5.4C2 Origin TN field to the TN of the reporting JU (a towed array is considered integral to the ship); if the detecting sensor is integral to another unit, track, or point being reported, C² JU sets the Origin TN field to the TN of the detecting unit, track, or point.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "2a. If contact is lost and the operator decides to report the track as a DATUM, C² JU reports a J3.4 message with the same Reference TN as the track for which contact has been lost, sets Data Report Type (DRT) = 4 (DATUM), sets ASW Time Function = 3 (Time Contact Lost) or 1 (Time Datum Established), sets Hour and Minute to the truncated time contact was lost or DATUM established, and includes Latitude, Longitude, and 15 Meters Depth; the decision to report a DATUM is an operator function.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 1, "content": "2b. If contact is regained after a DATUM, C² JU reports a J3.4 with DRT set to value 0, 1, or 2 using the same TN as the DATUM, or a new TN depending on operator action.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 2, "content": "2c. If another JU has already reported the contact under a Track Number and either a J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message containing the TN is received or a J3.4 message containing the TN has not been received for two consecutive periodic updates, C² JU may report the contact using that track number.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 3, "content": "2d. If C² JU believes a contact is the same contact reported by another JU using a different TN, C² JU may report it using a different TN; when this is done, only locally derived data shall be reported in the J3.4 message, and the J3.4 messages shall not contain data derived only by the reception of remote data from other IU(s) reporting the same contact.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 4, "content": "2e. If C² JU determines that a Subsurface IU is no longer active on the interface and C² JU also holds local data on the IU, C² JU assumes R² by reporting a J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message using the inactive IU address as the reference TN.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 5, "content": "2f. If further refined information concerning a subsurface fix or one of the other ASW points may result in a Subsurface surveillance track, C² JU reports the track with a new TN.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 6, "content": "2g. When associating Subsurface surveillance data, C² JU performs manual correlation of Subsurface surveillance data; the correlation procedures specified for Air, Surface (Maritime), or Land (Ground) tracks are not applied to Subsurface tracks.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 7, "content": "2h. If operational necessity requires a shorter wait time or none at all, an override is allowed; system design should also allow for longer wait times.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C189"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "exception_flow", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "1. If contact is lost while reporting a Subsurface surveillance track and the operator decides to report the track as a DATUM, C² JU reports a J3.4 message with the same Reference TN as the track for which contact has been lost, sets Data Report Type (DRT) = 4 (DATUM), sets ASW Time Function = 3 (Time Contact Lost) or 1 (Time Datum Established), sets Hour and Minute to the truncated time contact was lost or DATUM established, and includes Latitude, Longitude, and 15 Meters Depth; the decision to report a DATUM is an operator function. Exit: the DATUM report is sent as a J3.4 message.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C19", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "exception_flow", "audit_ordinal": 1, "content": "2. If contact is regained after a DATUM, C² JU reports a J3.4 with DRT set to value 0, 1, or 2 using the same TN as the DATUM, or a new TN depending on operator action. Exit: contact reporting resumes with the selected DRT and TN.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C19", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "exception_flow", "audit_ordinal": 2, "content": "3. If C² JU is not the first JU to report a contact and neither allowed exception occurs (a J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message containing the TN is received, or a J3.4 message containing the TN is not received for two consecutive periodic updates), C² JU shall not report the contact using that track number. Exit: C² JU may report what it believes to be the same contact using a different TN, and when this is done only locally derived data shall be reported in the J3.4 message.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C19", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "exception_flow", "audit_ordinal": 3, "content": "4. If C² JU determines that a Subsurface IU is no longer active on the interface and C² JU also holds local data on the IU, C² JU assumes R² by reporting a J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message using the inactive IU address as the reference TN. Exit: the J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message using the inactive IU address as the reference TN is sent.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P60#C195", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C19", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C146"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "Subsurface surveillance track information has been reported using the J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C19", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 1, "content": "Acoustic bearing/range information derived from ASW sensors has been exchanged using the Acoustic Bearing/Range message.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C19", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 2, "content": "For reported Subsurface surveillance tracks, the source of track data has been provided as the Source TN; established local tracks have been reported with all known parameters at the next reporting opportunity; and all data have been time tagged.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C19", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 3, "content": "The information on the track is as complete, accurate, and timely as possible, and the proper rules for reporting a track have been followed.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C19", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 4, "content": "For the Acoustic Bearing/Range report, the J5.4E0 Latitude and Longitude fields have been set to the position of the acoustic bearing origin, and bearings have been reported from the detecting sensor origin.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C19", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 5, "content": "For the Acoustic Bearing/Range report, if the detecting sensor is integral to the reporting JU, the J5.4C2 Origin TN field contains the TN of the reporting JU (a towed array is considered integral to the ship); if the detecting sensor is integral to another unit, track, or point being reported, the Origin TN field contains the TN of the detecting unit, track, or point.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C19", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 6, "content": "If contact was lost and the operator decided to report the track as a DATUM, a J3.4 message has been reported with the same Reference TN as the track for which contact has been lost, DRT = 4 (DATUM), ASW Time Function = 3 (Time Contact Lost) or 1 (Time Datum Established), Hour and Minute set to the truncated time contact was lost or DATUM established, and Latitude, Longitude, and 15 Meters Depth included.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C19", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 7, "content": "If contact was regained after a DATUM, a J3.4 message has been reported with DRT set to value 0, 1, or 2 using the same TN as the DATUM, or a new TN depending on operator action.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C19", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 8, "content": "If C² JU determined that a Subsurface IU is no longer active on the interface and C² JU also holds local data on the IU, C² JU has assumed R² by reporting a J3.4 Subsurface (Maritime) Track message using the inactive IU address as the reference TN.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C19", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 9, "content": "When C² JU reported what it believes to be the same contact using a different TN, only locally derived data have been reported in the J3.4 message, and the J3.4 messages do not contain data derived only by the reception of remote data from other IU(s) reporting the same contact.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C19", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 10, "content": "If C² JU was the first JU to report a contact, C² JU has assumed reporting responsibility for that Track Number.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P58#C190", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C182", "milstd6016b_sec4:P8#C19", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C180", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C198", "milstd6016b_sec4:P61#C197", "milstd6016b_sec4:P55#C183", "milstd6016b_sec4:P59#C193", "milstd6016b_sec4:P68#C215"], "valid_citation": true}], "empty_slots": [], "material_sha256": "2295efd3577e8991a9e6dbf8ac3c53963276cab9460171a23fa30d42cbb3872b"};
